#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""run_superWADERs: skipper-CCD images (and raw DAQ files) -> fits, clusters, cluster files and commissioning reports,
with superWADERs' own engine. No panaSKImg, and nothing from bin/run_WADERs or comm_scripts/src: every module it uses
is in this folder (engine/, clustering/, commissioning/).

    run_superWADERs INPUT [-o PARENT] [-j N] [options]      INPUT: an image, a raw DAQ file, or a .txt list of them
    run_superWADERs INPUT --campaign DIR [options]          add INPUT to the campaign DIR (data arriving in packets)
    run_superWADERs --campaign DIR                          no INPUT: open the campaign, with the review helper
    run_superWADERs -h            the flags;      run_superWADERs -h -v      the full guide

Every run is a campaign (commissioning/campaign.py): a new folder (superWADERs_<run name>/), or with --campaign DIR a
folder that grows packet by packet. An input already in the campaign (same path, size and modification time) is not
processed again; each run processes the new inputs, keeps their results (records/), rebuilds the pages of the tools
it was given from everything the campaign holds (the other tools keep theirs; --refresh-all rebuilds all), and the
campaign overview (index.html) of every tool. Without --campaign a run is on its own (a fresh folder with only its
inputs and tools), as before. Verdicts (pass / warn / fail) come from the criteria file the
campaign keeps (criteria.json; --criteria FILE to replace it, which re-judges everything without new fits).

What happens (one function each, called in order by main()):
  check_request         inputs exist, output folder free, option combinations valid (standard library only)
  ensure_environment    if this python lacks numpy / astropy / scipy / numba / ROOT, re-run inside the conda
                        environment that has them (the damic environment)
  raw_inputs            level-0 traces -> L0/ (decoded, checked, plotted); level-1 images -> L1/ FITS images with N
                        skips, which join the images
  packet_traces         --packet: level-0 traces / PSD traces of the packet -> records/packet/ (new ones only)
  to_process            the images not yet in the campaign (or changed, or missing a part a tool asks for)
  front_end             characterise every image and CCD before anything is fitted (engine/characterise.py): data form
                        (skip-resolved raw files are compressed first), geometry, dead / quiet channels, first-column
                        artefact, gain source, noise, dark charge, electron counting -> a clustering plan per CCD;
                        run-pooled dark charge for the Bayesian few-electron finder (images of one run setting)
  gain_correction       --gain-correction: fits of every CCD, g(n) curves per module / gain period / image
  process               per image one process (-j at a time, commissioning/worker.py): pedestal, the two
                        dark-current fits and the gain choice, calibration, per CCD the clustering chain (below),
                        cluster files in panaSKImg's format -> root/ (and root_gaincorr*/), and the image's record:
                        CCD metrics (commissioning/ccd_metrics.py), fit cards, packet / SR parts -> records/images*/
  composite             --composite: MakeComposite_Fe55_Clusters_Extensions.cc on the cluster files of this run
  render_all            from every record of the campaign: images/ (fits and CCD quality), packet/, dc_series/,
                        defects/ (only groups with a new image are made again), sr/; one overview page per tool
                        (<tool>/index.html: module x CCD grid, what needs attention, distributions, table, criteria)
                        and index.html (every tool per CCD)
  summary               summary.txt, fit_quality.csv, native_summary.json, characterisation/<image>.json

Clustering (--clusterer auto, the default), chosen per CCD after calibration and before clustering
(characterise.decide_ccd, on the numbers A_GMX itself uses):
  electron counting, sparse (core fill < 0.10)   A_GMX; inside it the Bayesian few-electron switch replaces A_GMX's
                                                 small clusters in sparse, low-dark-charge blocks (run-pooled dark
                                                 charge when the run setting has >= 2 images and DC <= 1.5e-2 e-/pix)
  electron counting, crowded (core fill >= 0.10) A_GMX crowded mode
  read noise >= 1 e-, or a structured background A_GMX 'unmodelled' (hysteresis on the calibrated image)
  flooded (no peaks, > 10 e-/pix)                threshold clusterer above the flooding level (subtracted per row),
                                                 at 10 / 30 x the charge width (not the read noise)
  peaks not resolved, not flooded                threshold clusterer (--thresholds; auto -> sigma0 rule there)
Every choice and every fallback is written to summary.txt, characterisation/<image>.json and each ROOT file.
"""
